# Unity ScriptableObject Data

All game data (creature parts, biomes, tech trees, weapon stats, catalogs) lives in ScriptableObjects or JSON — no hardcoded gameplay values in code.

**Locations:**

- `RoobsWorld/Assets/Data/` — ScriptableObject assets (CreatureParts, Biomes, TechTrees, Configs).
- Runtime-created catalogs (e.g. CreaturePartCatalog) may create ScriptableObject instances in code; persist to Assets when appropriate.

**Rules:**

- Use ScriptableObjects for design-time config and catalogs; use JSON for save data, creature DNA, and serialized state.
- Reference ScriptableObjects by asset or by instance; avoid duplicating data in code.
